<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sierra Leone Colony and Protectorate</h1><p class="st-meta">1792 CE – 1961 CE · capital Freetown</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British colony at Freetown, founded as a home for freed slaves, which became the base of the anti-slave-trade squadron and the cradle of Krio culture.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the failure of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-freedom">Province of Freedom</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone-company">Sierra Leone Company</a> brought about 1,100 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-loyalists">Black Loyalists</a> from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-clarkson">John Clarkson</a>, who founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freetown">Freetown</a> in 1792. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jamaican-maroons">Jamaican Maroons</a> arrived in 1800. The company could not pay its way, and in 1808 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> made the settlement a crown colony.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freetown">Freetown</a> became the base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> squadron suppressing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> and the seat of courts that freed captured slaves. Tens of thousands of these liberated Africans settled there, and with the earlier settlers formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone-creole-people">Krio people</a>, Protestant and English-educated. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourah-bay-college">Fourah Bay College</a>, founded in 1827, trained clergy and clerks for much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>. In 1896 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> declared a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> over the interior.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>A hut tax provoked the Hut Tax War of 1898, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bai-bureh">Bai Bureh</a>. Elections and constitutional reforms in the 1950s brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-margai">Milton Margai</a> to power, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a> became independent on 27 April 1961.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sierra-leone-colony-and-protectorate.jpg" alt="Sierra Leone Colony and Protectorate" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Pbroks13 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Sierra_Leone_(1916%E2%80%931961).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1792 CE – 1961 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Freetown</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>John Clarkson, Zachary Macaulay, Milton Margai</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestant Christianity, Sunni Islam, traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Krio, Temne, Mende</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sierra Leone colony, British Sierra Leone, Freetown Colony</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1876&amp;focus=sierra-leone-colony-and-protectorate" aria-label="Sierra Leone Colony and Protectorate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4314 1861 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sierra Leone Colony and Protectorate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4634 2117L4997 651M4634 2117L4634 2117"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M4634 2117h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4634 2117h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4634 2117h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Freetown. <a href="/atlas?year=1876&amp;focus=sierra-leone-colony-and-protectorate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside>